error[E0277]: `fn(Auth<ServiceKey>, Auth<Bearer>) -> impl Future<Output = NoContent> {both}` is not a Kynos handler
  --> tests/ui/antipattern/two_guards.rs:61:26
   |
61 |     is_handler::<App, _, _>(both);
   |                          ^ not a handler
   |
   = help: the trait `Handler<App, _>` is not implemented for fn item `fn(Auth<ServiceKey>, Auth<Bearer>) -> impl Future<Output = NoContent> {both}`
   = note: every argument must implement `Describe`, and `FromRequestParts` — or `FromRequest`, for the last one
   = note: a guard — `Auth`, `MaybeAuth` or `Scoped` — is the first argument, and there is at most one: combine schemes with `AnyOf` or `AllOf` instead
   = note: the return type must implement `IntoResponse` and `Responses`, and a codec such as `Json<T>` implements `Responses` only when `T` implements `Schema`: `#[derive(kynos::Schema)]` on `T` is the usual fix
   = note: the handler's future must be `Send`: nothing that is not — an `Rc`, a `RefCell` borrow, a lock guard — may be held across an `.await`
note: required by a bound in `is_handler`
  --> tests/ui/antipattern/two_guards.rs:58:24
   |
58 | fn is_handler<C, A, H: kynos::handler::Handler<C, A>>(_: H) {}
   |                        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ required by this bound in `is_handler`
